course: dictionary
lesson: 15607
title: Tapioca: a starch and a pudding
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word tapioca can name a starch, or a sweet pudding made with that starch. Read the words around it to find out which.
explain: «Mum thickened the soup with a spoon of tapioca flour.» Here the words thickened and soup show that tapioca is a powder that makes food thicker. «Ravi's drink had chewy tapioca pearls at the bottom.» Chewy and drink tell you tapioca means the small balls in a drink.
explain: «Lunch was tapioca pudding, a sweet milky pudding.» Sweet and milky tell you the pudding is made with tapioca. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence?
fact: Tapioca is a starch made from the root of the cassava plant.
fact: Tapioca comes as flour, flakes or small white balls called pearls.
fact: Tapioca pudding is a sweet, milky pudding made with tapioca pearls.
fact: Cassava grows in hot countries in South America, Africa and Asia.
fact: Tapioca pearls swell and go see-through when they are cooked, and tapioca flour is gluten-free.
exercise: «The soup was thickened with tapioca flour.» What is tapioca in this sentence? | *A starch from the cassava root, sold as flour | A hot, spicy sauce | A small green vegetable | A kind of bread
exercise: «Ravi's drink had chewy tapioca pearls at the bottom.» What are tapioca pearls? | Chopped fruit | *Small balls made from cassava starch | Wild rice from rivers | Sea creatures
exercise: Cassava grows in which kind of place? | A place with no sunlight at all | A cold, icy mountain | A deep, dark cave | *A hot country
test:
Tapioca pudding is a sweet, milky pudding. What is it made with? | Rice and cream | *Milk, sugar and tapioca pearls | Porridge oats and jam | Mashed potato and cheese
Tapioca pearls go see-through when cooked. What happens to them? | They turn black | *They swell and go see-through | They freeze solid | They shrink to dust
exam:
Tapioca flour is gluten-free. Why might someone with a gluten allergy choose it? | Because it has more gluten in it | *Because it contains no gluten | Because it is a type of meat | Because it only comes in tins
